# Real-LLM raw evidence stays local unless a redaction pass packages
# it. Raw per-case traces and raw per-run JSON eval reports both embed
# raw model `draft_text` / `draft_excerpt` content and are treated as
# raw evidence. The public-safe view is the redacted summary inside
# evidence_packs/financial_links_llm_v*/ and the matching cards/memos.
traces/local/llm_*/
reports/llm_adversarial_eval.json
reports/llm_adversarial_v1_eval.json
reports/llm_smoke_eval.json
# Adversarial v1 (12-case) LLM candidate raw eval reports. They embed raw
# model draft text; the public-safe view is the redacted summary inside
# evidence_packs/financial_links_llm_adversarial_v1/. The comparison card
# (reports/llm_adversarial_v1_candidate_v1_vs_v0_card.md) is public-safe and
# MAY be tracked, like the other LLM cards.
reports/llm_adversarial_v1_candidate_v0_eval.json
reports/llm_adversarial_v1_candidate_v1_eval.json

# Adversarial v2 (24-case) LLM candidate raw eval reports (M7b). Like v1 they
# embed raw model draft text; the public surfaces are the aggregate semantic-
# audit summary + the comparison card. The credential-free semantic replay
# fixture is a regenerable intermediate derived from the gitignored model/NLI
# decisions (which stay under reports/semantic_model_decisions/).
reports/llm_adversarial_v2_candidate_v0_eval.json
reports/llm_adversarial_v2_candidate_v1_eval.json
reports/llm_adversarial_v2_candidate_v1_semantic_replay_decisions.json
# M7 remediation candidate (llm_candidate_v2) — wired but not run. Same posture
# as v0/v1: raw eval report embeds model draft text; the replay-decision fixture
# is a regenerable intermediate. Both stay gitignored. The model/NLI decisions
# land under reports/semantic_model_decisions/ (already gitignored). The v2-vs-v1
# comparison card (reports/llm_adversarial_v2_candidate_v2_vs_v1_card.md) is
# intentionally NOT ignored: like the tracked v1-vs-v0 card it is public-safe
# (pass/fail counts only, same generate_eval_card.py), so it is meant to be
# committed after a credentialed run.
reports/llm_adversarial_v2_candidate_v2_eval.json
reports/llm_adversarial_v2_candidate_v2_semantic_replay_decisions.json
# M7 residual candidate (llm_candidate_v2_1) — wired but not run. Same posture:
# raw eval report embeds draft text; replay-decision fixture is a regenerable
# intermediate. The v2.1-vs-v2 card is public-safe (counts only) and trackable.
reports/llm_adversarial_v2_candidate_v2_1_eval.json
reports/llm_adversarial_v2_candidate_v2_1_semantic_replay_decisions.json
# M7 generalized residual candidate (llm_candidate_v2_2) — wired but not run.
reports/llm_adversarial_v2_candidate_v2_2_eval.json
reports/llm_adversarial_v2_candidate_v2_2_semantic_replay_decisions.json
# M7c held-out adversarial v3 — llm_candidate_v2.2 robustness run.
# Raw eval report embeds model draft text; replay-decision fixture is a
# regenerable intermediate. Both stay gitignored. The comparison card
# (reports/llm_adversarial_v3_candidate_v2_2_vs_improved_card.md) is
# public-safe (pass/fail counts only) and trackable after a credentialed run.
reports/llm_adversarial_v3_candidate_v2_2_eval.json
reports/llm_adversarial_v3_candidate_v2_2_semantic_replay_decisions.json
traces/local/llm_adversarial_v3_candidate_v2_2/
traces/local/llm_adversarial_v3_candidate_v2_2_semantic_model/
# M7e candidate-v2.3 (universal forward-looking ban) — wired, not run. Raw eval
# reports embed draft text; replay fixtures are regenerable intermediates. The
# v2.3-vs-v2.2 card is public-safe (counts only) and trackable.
reports/llm_adversarial_v2_candidate_v2_3_eval.json
reports/llm_adversarial_v2_candidate_v2_3_semantic_replay_decisions.json
reports/llm_adversarial_v3_candidate_v2_3_eval.json
reports/llm_adversarial_v3_candidate_v2_3_semantic_replay_decisions.json
traces/local/llm_adversarial_v2_candidate_v2_3/
traces/local/llm_adversarial_v2_candidate_v2_3_semantic_model/
traces/local/llm_adversarial_v3_candidate_v2_3/
traces/local/llm_adversarial_v3_candidate_v2_3_semantic_model/
# Consent-overflag calibration intermediates for v2.3-v3 (regenerable from raw
# decisions). The clearance LOG (reports/..._consent_calibration.{json,md}) is
# public-safe and tracked.
reports/semantic_model_decisions/adversarial_v3_llm_candidate_v2_3_calibrated.json
reports/llm_adversarial_v3_candidate_v2_3_calibrated_semantic_replay_decisions.json
traces/local/llm_adversarial_v3_candidate_v2_3_calibrated_semantic_model/
# M7d grader-reliability: raw credentialed verdicts embed draft-quoting
# rationale/evidence_spans; the public-safe verdict fixture is a regenerable
# intermediate. The reliability REPORT (reports/grader_gold_reliability.md) and
# result JSON are public-safe and meant to be tracked after a real pass; the
# demo outputs are illustrative and regenerable, so they stay ignored.
reports/grader_gold/
reports/grader_gold_reliability_demo.json
reports/grader_gold_reliability_demo.md

# Repeat-run aggregation demo outputs from the variance-report-fixture
# Make target. The fixture inputs under tests/fixtures/llm_repeats/ are
# tracked; the rendered demo outputs are not, so the target can be
# re-run without polluting the tree.
reports/llm_repeat_summary_fixture.md
reports/llm_repeat_summary_fixture.json

# Opt-in model/NLI semantic-grader outputs. These are generated local
# decision/eval artifacts from credentialed model calls; publish only
# after an explicit evidence-pack/redaction decision.
reports/semantic_model_decisions/
reports/*_semantic_model_eval.json
reports/*semantic_model_reporting_surface.html
traces/local/*_semantic_model/

# Credentialed repeat-run capture outputs. Raw per-run eval reports
# embed raw model draft text and are treated as raw evidence; raw
# traces ditto. The aggregated public-safe summary
# (reports/llm_repeat_summary.{md,json}) MAY be tracked because it
# carries only counts / distributions / public-safe identifiers; the
# aggregator's tests verify the no-raw-draft / no-raw-trace-path
# invariant.
reports/llm_repeats/

# Credential-free replay of the semantic regression seeds. The report +
# deterministic improved_v0 traces are regenerable check outputs (they
# embed a deterministic draft_excerpt); the tracked fixture
# (regressions_semantic_adversarial_v1_decisions.json) + the hermetic
# test are the durable artifacts. Regenerate with
# `make regression-replay-adversarial-v1-semantic`.
reports/regression_semantic_adversarial_v1_eval.json
traces/local/regression_semantic_adversarial_v1/
# Adversarial v2 semantic-regression replay (M7): same as v1 — the report +
# deterministic improved_v0 traces are regenerable check outputs; the tracked
# fixture (regressions_semantic_adversarial_v2_decisions.json) + the hermetic
# test are the durable artifacts. Regenerate with
# `make regression-replay-adversarial-v2-semantic`.
reports/regression_semantic_adversarial_v2_eval.json
traces/local/regression_semantic_adversarial_v2/
# M7 grader-calibration replay: the report + deterministic improved_v0 traces are
# regenerable check outputs; the tracked fixtures
# (calibration_semantic_adversarial_v2.jsonl + ..._decisions.json) + the hermetic
# test are the durable artifacts. Regenerate with
# `make calibration-replay-adversarial-v2-semantic`.
reports/calibration_semantic_adversarial_v2_eval.json
traces/local/calibration_semantic_adversarial_v2/
